# Stage 14 O-10 fix — frozen MCP-server snapshot is SHA-pinned (LF bytes).
#
# tests/src/praxis/contract_tests/ports/test_mcp_jsonrpc_golden.py pins
# STDIO_SHA256 over the *bytes* of src/stdio.ts in this frozen snapshot. The
# blob is LF in git's index, but Windows core.autocrlf smudges it to CRLF on
# checkout, so the working-copy byte hash diverged from the pinned LF hash
# (the O-10 red). Forcing eol=lf for the whole frozen snapshot makes the
# working copy match the index + the pinned SHA on every platform. The tree is
# immutable reference material (all text), so this is purely a checkout-eol pin.
tests/reference/spike-mcp-server-snapshot-d93f71a/** text eol=lf
